1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Welcome to the interactive design and operational platform-for planar flexible manufacturing: Tile Glider.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Researchers can monitor and sort experiments across 24 critical metrics including mover allocations, solver models, and status.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Opening Experiment Details provides full visibility into configuration parameters, layouts, and orders.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:21,000
The Layout tab renders the factory grid twin. Hovering reagents dynamically illuminates their physical dispensers.

5
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:29,000
For finished runs, Tile Glider runs directly inside the modal for instant visual validation.

6
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:37,000
Domain modeling supports pharmaceuticals and complex perfumes with scent notes, viscosity, and volatility.

7
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Custom recipes are sequenced with drag-and-drop ordering and quick insertion of physical Mixers and Cappers.

8
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:57,000
The visual Layout Studio generates industrial lines, loops, rings, and custom grids with drag-and-drop editing.

9
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Fine-tune solvers from Hexaly to CPLEX Medicine with configurable batch sizes and warmup modes.

10
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,000
The Batch Matrix engine computes Cartesian product sweeps with dry-run compatibility checks.

11
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Now entering Tile Glider, the dedicated visual simulator for planar transport systems.

12
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Launching Simulation 4, featuring 12 movers, 64 tiles, and 99 patient orders.

13
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:49,000
Spring-physics animations provide smooth centered mover travel across speed presets.

14
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:58,000
The frame scrubber enables instant timeline seeking with dynamic 50-shade thermal heatmap accumulation.

15
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Multi-mover stack detection displays fanned offsets and counter badges, fully synchronized with live Gantt telemetry.

16
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:11,000
Complete end-to-end control from experiment configuration to visual telemetry.

